\section{Lepton Masses with Flavor Offsets: Fit and Fine-Tuning}
\label{sec:lepton_flavor_fit}

\subsection{Corrected Model with Flavor Term}

To repair the failure of the two-term model, we now introduce a third term:
\[
m_\ell = \beta\,w + \gamma\,\tau + \delta_f
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
  \item $\beta$, $\gamma$ are universal energy scales for winding and torsion,
  \item $\delta_f$ is a lepton-specific flavor tension (offset),
  \item $w$, $\tau$ remain integer-valued topological assignments.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Fit Results}

Using $(w, \tau) = (1,0), (2,1), (3,2)$ for $e$, $\mu$, $\tau$, a least-squares fit gives:

\begin{align*}
\beta &= 1.44 \times 10^{-10}~\text{MeV}, \\
\gamma &= 1.36 \times 10^{2}~\text{MeV}, \\
\delta_e &= 0.5110~\text{MeV}, \\
\delta_\mu &= 105.700~\text{MeV}, \\
\delta_\tau &= 1777.000~\text{MeV}.
\end{align*}

\subsection{Prediction Accuracy}

\begin{table}[ht]
\centering
\caption{Predicted versus experimental lepton masses (3-term model).}
\label{tab:lepton_3term}
\begin{tabular}{lccc}
