The match is effectively exact.

\subsection{Interpretation and Fine-Tuning Diagnosis}

\paragraph{Strength.} This model demonstrates that the SAT framework, when extended to include lepton-specific energy contributions $\delta_f$, can reproduce the full lepton mass hierarchy to arbitrary precision.

\paragraph{Limitation.} However, the success is diagnostic rather than predictive:
\begin{itemize}
  \item There are 5 fit parameters for only 3 outputs — the system is overdetermined.
  \item The flavor offsets $\delta_f$ are unconstrained by SAT geometry and behave as free parameters.
  \item The model exhibits no compression of information or derivation of the flavor sector.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Conclusion.}
This result constitutes a \emph{fine-tuned fit}. It validates the SAT energy structure but highlights the lack of a principled flavor mechanism. The flavor offsets $\delta_f$ function as patches, not predictions.

\subsection{Next Step}

Future modules must derive $\delta_f$ from first principles — e.g., via filament defect topology, vacuum embedding asymmetry, or SAT-based symmetry breaking — to elevate this from an empirical fit to a falsifiable prediction.

