\subsection*{III.C.4 Cumulative Quantities: Mass and Entropy Analogs}

We define two integral quantities:

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Cumulative Intersection Count:}
  \begin{equation}
  I(R) = \int_0^R \rho_{\text{link}}(r) \cdot 4\pi r^2 \, dr
  \end{equation}
  representing the total number of resolved topological interactions, i.e., the projection imprint analogous to mass.

  \item \textbf{Cumulative Angular Work:}
  \begin{equation}
  W(R) = \int_0^R \rho_{\text{link}}(r) \cdot \theta_4(r) \cdot 4\pi r^2 \, dr
  \end{equation}
  representing the total angular load resolved by $\Sigma_t$, analogous to entropy or curvature accumulation.
\end{itemize}

