\subsection*{III.C.5 Cosmological Phases as Projection Geometry}

The PGCU model naturally reproduces key cosmological epochs:

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Pre-Resolution Phase ($R \ll 1$):} Low intersection, high angles — projection nearly frozen.
  \item \textbf{Resolution Epoch ($R \sim R_{\text{peak}}$):} Maximal intersection rate, $\theta_4 \approx 90^\circ$ — peak curvature and mass imprint.
  \item \textbf{Post-Resolution Phase ($R > R_{\text{peak}}$):} Declining resistance — projection accelerates (analogous to dark energy era).
  \item \textbf{Asymptotic Phase ($R \gg 1$):} No remaining filaments intersected — projection coasts in flat geometry.
\end{itemize}

